Before looking more in detail, I'd like to already say that InstantSearchSSRProvider is designed for one having a single InstantSearch component as its child. We should have a warning (or maybe even error) if there are multiple, as they will share the states.

The pattern you may be looking for could be "multiple root indices":

```jsx
const searchClient = algoliasearch();
searchFn = searchClient.search;
searchClient.search = (queries) => {
  queries.shift();
  return searchFn(queries).then(({ results }) => ({
    results: [
      {
        hits: [],
        nbHits: 0,
        nbPages: 0,
        page: 0,
        processingTimeMS: 0,
        hitsPerPage: 0,
        exhaustiveNbHits: false,
        query: '',
        params: '',
      },
      ...results,
    ],
  }));
};

function App() {
  return (
    <InstantSearch indexName="_root_index_" searchClient={searchClient}>
      <Index indexName="1" />
      <Index indexName="2" />
    </InstantSearch>
  );
}
```

Index 1 and index 2 will not share any state in this setup.
